It is a terminology issue, on page 38 of his PhD, Bart Barenbrug defines the Jacobian as:<br><br>Jacobian dC/dR as 'dependency between constraint error and restriction value (impulse/force etc).<br><br>Indeed, it is a unit-impulse method to measure the effective mass, given you know the axis/direction in the right space.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Wed Mar 21, 2007 6:41 pm</p><hr />
