Erin, apart from those 2 methods I think there is a 3rd popular method to compute Jacobian: <br><br>Empirical: measuring the effect of applying a unit-impulse.  It is mentioned in <a href="http://home.iae.nl/users/starcat/dynamo" class="postlink">Bart Barenbrug PhD thesis and Dynamo library</a>.<br><br>I've seen some people using this in combination with Featurestone-style constraint solving.<br><br>Have you tried that?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Wed Mar 21, 2007 3:57 pm</p><hr />
